export const modernPerspective = [
  'A pseudopotential or PAW dataset is a versioned scientific input. Its exchange–correlation functional, valence and semicore configuration, core radii, reference states, nonlinear-core treatment, scalar-relativistic or fully relativistic construction, projector channels, generator, and file version can materially change a calculation. A library label such as “recommended” does not replace validation for the target system and observable.',
  'Plane-wave cutoff convergence tests the numerical representation for one chosen dataset. It does not prove that the dataset reproduces the corresponding all-electron atom, transfers to a different oxidation or spin state, contains the required semicore states, or is reliable for a core-sensitive observable. Representation convergence and pseudopotential transferability are separate questions.',
